  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\nThe Erd\u0151s minimum overlap problem involves optimizing a non-convex potential with a complex correlation structure. I propose a hybrid quantum-inspired classical optimization strategy to escape local optima. Key innovations:\n   - Quantum-inspired momentum embedding to maintain gradient direction history\n   - Multi-stage spectral decomposition to separate coarse/fine frequency modes\n   - Targeted Lagrange multiplier evolution to maintain constraint satisfaction exactly\n   - Destructive interference filtering in the overlap domain to avoid expensive operations\n\nThis approach fundamentally differs by embedding constraints into the optimization direction rather than extracting them separately, focusing on destructive constructive interference avoidance.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\nTensorized formulation:\nVariable: h \u2208 R^n (grid samples) with h_i \u2208 [0,1]\nConstraint: \u2211_i h_i = n/2 (integral normalization)\nObjective: minimize max_l (compute_corr(h)[l]) * (2/n)\n\nProjected Gradient evolution:\n\u2207_h [max_l corr_l] + \u03bc(h) * (n - 2\u2211_i h_i)\nwhere \u03bc(h) is a projected penalty multiplier\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\nPhase 0: Initialization\n    n_start = 400\n    h0 = interpolate_to(initial_h_values, n_start, target=200) if parent exists\n    h0 = project_feasible(h0/2*len(h0), target=n_start/2)\n\nPhase 1: Feature decomposition\n    U = np.fft.fft(compute_corr(h0))\n    l_freqs = np.argsort(|U|)[:n_start//2]  # Most energetic modes\n    mapping: lag to frequency index\n\nPhase 2: Quantum-inspired optimization\n    h_new = h0.copy()\n    for iteration in range(max_steps):\n        if time_exceeded: break\n        corr = compute_corr(h_new)\n        c_max = np.max(corr) * (2/n_start)\n        directed_qubit = np.angle(np.fft.hfft(h_new))\n        \n        # Destructive interference filter\n        filter_func = abs(np.fft.rfft(corr)) > c_max/3\n            \n        # Momentum-based gradient\n        g_best = np.zeros(n_start)\n        for lag in range(len(corr)):\n            if abs(corr[lag]) > c_max/5 and lag in l_freqs:\n                sign = 1 if corr[lag] > 0 else -1\n                shift_idx = mapping[lag]\n                weight = np.exp(2*time_survived)\n                g_best[shift_idx] += sign * weight * h_new[shift_idx] * 0.1\n                \n        # Constraint-aware projection\n        \u03a3 = diagonalize(project_penalty_matrix(h_new, target))\n        h_new = H_step(h_new - g_best, \u03a3)  # Modified quantum gate operation\n\nPhase 3: Lagrange recovery enforcement\n    \u03bc = np.max(compute_corr(h_new)) * 5  # Adaptive lambda\n    while |\u2211h_new - target| > 0.1:\n        diff = target - \u2211h_new\n        h_new += diff/len(h_new) * smoothing_factor\n\nPhase 4: Resolution doubling (if time permits)\n    n_next = n_start * 2\n    mapping_idx = generate_grid_mapping(n_start, n_next)\n    h_refined = np.zeros(n_next)\n    for i in range(n_start):\n        if not np.isnan(h_new[i]):\n            h_refined[mapping_idx[i]] += h_new[i]*(n_next/n_start)\n\n4. Search Choices and Variations\nDefault Configuration:\n    - Resolution path: [400, 800] \n    - Energy filter threshold: 0.03 (measures min significant correlation energy)\n    - Momentum retention factor: 0.7 (fraction of previous gradient preserved)\n\nTriggered Configuration:\n    - LowFrequencyMode(params) Auto-activate if |median(corr)| > 0.15\n    - DestructiveFilter activates if detected improvements stall\n\n5. Compute Budget and Robustness\nEstimation: Mode decomposition (FFT) and diagonalization require O(n\u00b2) operations. Critical sections:\n    - Mode decomposition: \u223c100ms/n_points\n    - Quantum gate projection: \u223c500ms/n_points\n    - Deadline checkpoint: placed before hazardous filtering operations\n\nRecovery Strategy:\nFalls to gradient descent: random_half_reflection(initial_h) -> project to bounds\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract\n    - Verify: sum(h_final)*dx \u2248 1\n    - Check: min(h) >= 0; max(h) <= 1\n    - Compute C5 = max(compute_corr(h)) * (2/n)\n    - Compare to parent solution: must show improvement\n    - Reject if: max(compute_corr) > 1E-3 (significantly nois)\n    - Roundtrip projection: h_final = project_feasible(h_final, target)",
